---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

import AudioPlayer from '../components/AudioPlayer.astro';
import audio from '../assets/audio/adelheid.mp3';
---

<PageLayout title='FAQ' description=`Frequently asked questions.`>
	<Fragment slot="page-header">FAQ</Fragment>
	<article slot="page-content">
		<h2>How is 'Adelheid' pronounced?</h2>
		<p>Press the audio icon below to hear the pronunciation.</p>
		<span style="display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle; margin-top: 1rem;"><AudioPlayer audioSrc={audio}/></span>
		<div style="display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle; margin-top: 1rem;">
			<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column;">
				<span style="font-size: 1.802rem; font-weight: 600;">a·del·heid</span>
				<span style="font-size: 1rem;">/ˈædəlhaɪd/</span>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2>What is your stance on privacy?</h2>
		<p>We believe that privacy is an inalienable right that must always be respected. While data is often useful for improving products and gathering feedback, we believe this data should be given voluntarily and as anonymously as possible, while still giving you control over how we deal with personalized data.</p>
		<p>You can read more in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

		<h2>What is your stance on Web3, NFTs, and blockchain technology?</h2>
		<p>We strongly oppose anything and everything related to blockchain technology. The space is rife with scams and fails to solve any real problems.</p>
		<p>We will never utilize or endorse any kind of blockchain technology.</p>

		<h2>What is your stance on machine learning and generative AI?</h2>
		<p>We are not generally against the idea. We believe that machine learning is an incredibly useful field of research with tons of untapped potential in the gaming sphere. Namely, we believe it has extreme potential to greatly enhance actual NPC AI and make for much more fun and engaging experiences. In addition, machine learning is amazing at optimization problems and is incredibly useful in that area.</p>
		<p>When it comes to generative AI, we believe that it can be useful for software development, but we don't find it suitable for any other use. While we do believe that LLM tooling is a very useful tool for programming, we do not believe it is useful or generally ethical to use it for any other purpose. We believe it is important for human artists, writers, and designers to be able to be successful in the industry; software engineers can be successful regardless of whether LLMs assist them, but for other job roles this is not so much the case. Even with its use in software development, we believe it must be used responsibly and as a supplementary tool, not as a replacement for critical thinking or architectural design. We also believe all AI-generated code must be heavily reviewed by humans before including it in production applications. As such, we believe that generative AI and LLMs are incredibly useful as tools to enhance real human work, but it should never replace human creators.</p>
		<p>We do not support the usage of generative AI or LLMs at any point in the pipeline of creating assets, including but not limited to non-code textual assets, and all graphical assets. As such, we have absolutely no plans to ever include AI-generated content (meaning anything non-code) in any of our games, nor at any point in the pipeline of creating a game. For programming, we believe it is a useful supplementary tool and may or may not use it specifically for that purpose.</p>

		<h2>What is your stance on Stop Killing Games?</h2>
		<p>We fully support the Stop Killing Games initiative. We are fully committed to ensuring our games are always playable and available, even after we are long gone.</p>

		<h2>Why don't you have Twitter? What's Bluesky?</h2>
		<p>We firmly believe that Twitter as a platform stands against our values of community and openness, and that the platform itself has become uninclusive and abusive.</p>
		<p><a href="https://bsky.social/about">Bluesky</a> is a social media platform similar to Twitter, developed on the <a href="https://atproto.com/">AT Protocol</a>. The platform was originally created by Twitter and is now independently run by former Twitter employees. We believe that Bluesky reflects the values that Twitter once stood for, and is a much better, more inclusive platform for us to engage with our community on.</p>

		<h2>Why don't you have Instagram, Facebook, or Threads?</h2>
		<p>Due to our stance on privacy, we do not find any of these platforms suitable to be on.</p>

		<h2>Why aren't your games or software available on MacOS?</h2>
		<p>It's not that we don't want to, but Apple currently makes it prohibitively expensive and difficult to publish and distribute games and software on MacOS. In addition, the market for our games and software isn't very large on MacOS. For those reasons, we have no current plans to release games or software on any operating systems Apple owns and controls, but this is subject to change in the future.</p>
	</article>
</PageLayout>
